UPDATE `user_settings` SET `setting_value` = '<p>Kendrick Lamar is set to close out Glastonbury as the festival''s final <a href="https://www.search.com/web?q=headliner">headliner</a> the \n\\nday after Sir Paul McCartney delivered an explosive history-making \n\\nset.</p> <p>The US rapper will be the last performer to take to \n\\nthe Pyramid Stage on Sunday, concluding the festivities at \n\\nWorthy Farm in Somerset.</p> <p>Soul singer Diana Ross \n\\nis also on the bill for the final day as she fills the \n\\nSunday teatime legends <a href="https://jandaqq.blogspot.com/">agen slot mudah menang</a>.</p> <p>Lamar''s upcoming \n\\nshow on the main stage will mark his Glastonbury debut.</p> <p>He is expected to \n\\nplay a range of hit tracks including songs from his recently released fifth studio album Mr Morale & The Big \n\\nSteppers.</p> <p>It was announced in 2020 that the Grammy-winning singer would \n\\nheadline Glastonbury''s 50th anniversary edition but the festival has \n\\nfaced two years of delays due to the pandemic.</p> <p>The Pyramid Stage will host an array of \n\\ntalent before Lamar including Lorde, Elbow, Herbie Hancock, DakhaBrakha and Black Dyke Band.</p> <p>There will also be musical stars across the festival''s multiple stages with the Pet \n\\nShop Boys and Years & Years performing on the Other \n\\nStage.</p> <p>While electronic duo Bicep will headline the West Holts Stage, Charli XCX will close the John Peel \n\\nStage and Imelda May and McFly will both play the \n\\nAvalon Stage.</p> <p>On Saturday evening, Sir Paul delivered a Glastonbury headline set for the \n\\nhistory books which included surprise appearances from Bruce Springsteen and Foo Fighters frontman Dave Grohl.</p> <p>As he took to the Pyramid Stage, the former Beatle became the festival''s \n\\noldest solo headliner, a week after he celebrated his \n\\n80th birthday.</p> <p>To mark the momentous occasion, \n\\nSir Paul treated the masses in the crowd to a selection of his own songs \n\\nas well as beloved tracks by The Beatles and from his later group Wings.</p> <p>During his more than two hour set, he played a range \n\\nof classics songs including Hey Jude, Blackbird, Live \n\\nAnd Let Die, Ob-La-Di, Ob"La"Da and Get Back.</p> <p>The electrifying show \n\\nwas further amplified as he introduced Grohl to the stage to sing I Saw Her Standing There \n\\nand Band On The Run.</p> <p>It was his first public performance \n\\nsince the death of his Foo Fighters bandmate, drummer Taylor Hawkins.</p> <p>Following Grohl, Sir Paul announced he had another surprise all the way \n\\nfrom the east coast of America as Springsteen took \n\\nto the stage to play Glory Days and I Wanna Be Your Man with him.</p> <p>Sir Paul \n\\nalso remembered his nearest and dearest during the headline set \n\\nincluding dedicating a piano-led version of My Valentine to his wife Nancy, \n\\nSomething to his Beatles'' bandmate George Harrison and Here Today to John Lennon.</p> <p>As \n\\npart of the encore, through special technology which could isolate Lennon''s vocals from old \n\\nrecordings, Sir Paul was able to duet The Beatles'' track I''ve Got A Feeling alongside his former bandmate on the \n\\nPyramid Stage.</p> <p>To end the historic set he sang The Beatles'' song \n\\nThe End to a cheering crowd with Springsteen and Grohl also returning to provide guitar solos.</p> <p>Despite the majority of the Glastonbury headline performances being shown live \n\\non the BBC iPlayer, Sir Paul was not aired on the broadcaster''s channels \n\\nuntil an hour into his set.</p> <p>In a statement, the BBC said: "This year we are delighted to bring audiences our most extensive coverage of Glastonbury to date.</p> <p>"Paul McCartney''s much anticipated \n\\nset was broadcast on BBC One at 10.30pm as well as \n\\non Radio 2 and will be available on BBC iPlayer and BBC Sounds.</p> <p>"Due to the complexity of broadcasting an event of this scale and the volume of performances we cover, there is sometimes variation between performances taking place and their transmission."</p> \n\\n<p>Earlier on Saturday, the Pyramid Stage hosted a speech by Greta Thunberg where she called on society to take on its \n\\n"historic responsibility to set things right" with the global \n\\nclimate crisis.</p> <p>Ms Thunberg''s speech was followed by a set by pop rock band Haim, with Noel Gallagher''s High Flying Birds taking to the Pyramid Stage after them.</p> <p>The Pyramid Stage also hosted \n\\nmusical stars Haim, AJ Tracey, Easy Life, Joy Crookes and Les \n\\nAmazones d''Afrique on Saturday.</p> <p>US pop star Olivia Rodrigo and rapper Megan Thee Stallion both played on the \n\\nOther Stage,  situs slot terbaik while Mercury-winner Celeste played the <a href="https://www.britannica.com/search?query=West%20Holts">West Holts</a> Stage.</p> \n\\n<p>Eilish gave an electrifying headline performance on the Pyramid Stage on Friday \n\\nto end the first day of performances at Glastonbury.</p> <p>Her \n\\nappearance was another landmark moment for the festival as \n\\nshe became Glastonbury''s youngest ever solo headliner.</p></div>\n\\n\n\\n<!-- ad: website --><img src="http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-JVNzCfCLR0g/VqB2fLJMkzI/AAAAAAAAAlI/bJkdMeKSMX4/s1600/645546546456546.jpg" alt="Rekomendasi Agen Judi Bola, Poker, Dan Togel Online Indonesia" style="max-width:450px;float:right;padding:10px 0px 10px 10px;border:0px;">' WHERE `user_id` = '4350' AND `locale` = 'en_US' AND `setting_name` = 'biography' AND `assoc_type` = '0' AND `assoc_id` = '0';
